# Line-ending policy.
#
# The repository stores every text file with LF, and checks it out with LF on
# every platform. This replaces the previous reliance on each developer's
# `core.autocrlf` setting, which silently produced CRLF working-tree files on
# Windows while the committed blobs stayed LF. Any tool that rewrote a file
# with LF — Node's `writeFile`, cargo, most editors — then left it permanently
# "modified" in `git status` with an empty `git diff`, which blocked
# `git pull --ff-only` and broke the byte-exact comparison in
# `scripts/render_mobile_design_system.mjs` check mode.
#
# Rust, Node, Vite, and PowerShell all read LF sources correctly on Windows,
# so LF everywhere is safe; the two exceptions below are declared explicitly.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shell entry points. cmd.exe is the least tolerant consumer in the
# toolchain, so these keep CRLF in the working tree.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never convert line endings, never attempt a text diff.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
